# Day 45

## Experiment Title

Deploying Docker Containers using GitHub Actions


## Objective

To understand how GitHub Actions can be used for automated Docker container deployment.


## Theory

GitHub Actions supports Continuous Deployment by automating the deployment of Docker containers after successful workflow execution. Deployment automation reduces manual effort and improves application delivery speed.

Using GitHub Actions, developers can automate container deployment processes such as image pulling, container execution, and deployment verification.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Docker Desktop

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Access the GitHub Actions workflow configuration file.

Configure deployment steps for Docker containers.

Commit and push the workflow file to the repository.

Observe workflow execution and deployment activity.

Verify successful container deployment after workflow completion.


## Output

Docker container deployment was automated successfully using GitHub Actions.

The workflow executed deployment steps successfully.

Application containers were deployed properly after workflow execution.


## Result

Successfully performed automated Docker container deployment using GitHub Actions.
